// Project settings for Zed. Deliberately minimal: it carries only what is specific to
// THIS repo, so it never overrides a preference set in your user settings.
//
// Its one job is to stop the editor reformatting files away from how they are written.
// Zed formats YAML, JSON and Markdown with its bundled Prettier, and Prettier's
// tabWidth, printWidth and useTabs follow Zed's tab_size, preferred_line_length and
// hard_tabs unless set in a "prettier" object. tab_size defaults to 4 and
// preferred_line_length to 80, so an unconfigured Zed re-indents this repo's 2-space
// YAML to 4 and breaks lines it should leave alone.
//
// Not set on purpose:
//   format_on_save - left to your user settings. Formatting stays manual; nothing in CI
//                    gates it, so this file is the only thing keeping the editor honest.
//   formatter      - Zed's default "auto" already picks Prettier for every language here.
//                    Disallowing Prettier for Markdown below is enough to stop it: with
//                    no Markdown language server installed, "auto" then finds nothing.
{
  // This repo is 2-space indented throughout - shell, JSON, YAML, Markdown. Setting
  // these two is what makes Prettier's output match, because they are the documented
  // source for its tabWidth and printWidth.
  //
  // 100 rather than 80 because every workflow pins its actions by SHA, and
  // `- uses: <action>@<40-char-sha> # <version>` reaches 96 characters
  // (.github/workflows/release-please.yml). 100 also keeps the twelve compact
  // `{ "type": ..., "section": ... }` entries in release-please-config.json on one line
  // each; the longest is 82 characters, so Prettier at 80 would explode every one of
  // them onto four lines.
  //
  // Lines past 100 do exist, but Prettier cannot touch them: they are inside `run: |`
  // and `body: |` block scalars, which it never reflows, and the 100-character $schema
  // URL in release-please-config.json, which is a single string it cannot break.
  "tab_size": 2,
  "preferred_line_length": 100,

  "languages": {
    // Pinned again here, not just derived from the two settings above, because a
    // language-specific value REPLACES the top-level one entirely rather than merging
    // with it. Should Zed ever ship a YAML tab_size default, the derivation above stops
    // reaching YAML; this does not.
    //
    // Verified honored at project level: formatting a 4-space file reindents it to 2 and
    // leaves the 93-character `uses:` line in .github/workflows/sonarcloud.yml intact,
    // which requires printWidth >= 93. Worth stating because Zed documents project
    // settings only as "editor behavior and language tooling options like tab_size,
    // formatter, and format_on_save" - it does not name the prettier key.
    //
    // singleQuote is already Prettier's default. It is stated so the repo's quote style
    // is declared rather than inherited, and cannot move with a future Prettier default.
    // Consequence: `cron: '0 6 * * 1'` in update-lazydocker.yml becomes
    // `cron: "0 6 * * 1"` the next time that file is formatted. That matches the six
    // double-quoted scalars in .github/dependabot.yml and docs/_config.yml.
    "YAML": {
      "prettier": {
        "allowed": true,
        "tabWidth": 2,
        "printWidth": 100,
        "singleQuote": false
      }
    },

    // Markdown is turned off rather than widened: the prose here is hand-wrapped and
    // runs past 300 columns in places (docs/index.md, CHANGELOG.md), so there is no
    // printWidth that makes Prettier a no-op. Reflowing it would rewrite every file.
    //
    // JSON gets no entry of its own. Prettier handles it at the width above, which is
    // what keeps release-please-config.json intact. One known consequence: Prettier
    // collapses any array that fits inside printWidth and has no option to keep one
    // expanded - the "respect the author's line break" heuristic covers objects only -
    // so the "deny" list in wsl/user/.claude/settings.json becomes a single 83-character
    // line the first time that file is formatted. Preserving it would need printWidth
    // <= 82, which is also the exact minimum release-please-config.json needs; the two
    // constraints meet on a single value with no slack either way, so JSON is left to
    // Prettier rather than balanced on one character.
    "Markdown": {
      "prettier": {
        "allowed": false
      }
    }
  }
}
